ipt manipulations beyond just plain HTML structure.\n\nIt’s also worth noting that modern accessibility best practices often recommend avoiding inline styles and opting for explicit styling through the use of CSS rather than directly embedding stylings within HTML content; this way, they are easily reusable across multiple instances of the page.\n:mdquo:\n  . :mdquo:\n\nIf your goal was solely to present visually how such combination might appear without needing a particular structural nesting pattern, then the original markup remains functional. If considering a real-world application scenario where presentation should be governed independently from content semantics, adopting proper HTML structure and possibly external styling may provide better results.", "depth": 1, "seed_id": 3481, "token_count": 512}
